  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Rain moving in from the west with locally heavy\nrainfall possible over central and northern portions of the \narea early this morning. Flooding is not expected.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nOccluded front sitting just to the east of James Bay and the\nOntario/Quebec border as of 05z. Most of the heavy rain is just\nnow entering into nw portions of the CWA. This looks to be the \nco-located with the low-level jet and gradient of higher pwats \nper latest TPW satellite imagery. Guidance is now indicating \nthis will shift east thru 12z this morning. At the same time \nsurface boundary enhancing lift in srn Quebec, just to the north\nof New England and expect this to track into the Central \nHighlands within the next 2-3 hours. As it heads into the \nwestern Maine mountains orographic may help enhance heavy \nrainfall early this morning thus have kept heaviest totals thru \n12z over the Central Highlands. \n\nLLJ pushes east into NB by 15z this morning with steady rain\ncoming to an end. However with front still lingering back to the\nwest there will be plenty of forcing to keep showers going over\nmost of the area this afternoon and evening.  \n\nHave continued with trend of prior shift with slgt chc to lochc\npops this afternoon and evening before increasing to likely\ntonight as coastal low rides to the south of the waters\novernight. Patchy fog expected over most of the area tonight as\noccluded front pretty much dies in place. Downeast likely to see\nareas of fog late tonight with humid airmass remaining in place. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Chance for showers Wednesday afternoon into\nThursday as a cold front crosses the area.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION... As the low pressure system exits \nover the Maritimes, the next low pressure system centered over \nthe Hudson Bay begins to track E. The associated cold front is \nexpected to move into the region Wednesday evening and exit \nThursday afternoon. Ensemble models have been trending towards a\ndrier solution with isolated showers. Little QPF is expected \nwith these showers. There is a possibility for a few rumbles of \nthunder but nothing severe.",
